  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward thermally manipulating ordered, dual-phase Al-containing HEAs. In particular, R9 and R16 establish thermal exposure or annealing of AlCoCrFeNi2.1, while R17 identifies temperature-dependent ordering and a sharp phase-separation event near 600°C in closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys. R15 links chemical order and antiphase-boundary formation to dislocation strengthening, and R18 indicates that cross-slip can relieve stress and suppress localization. Several records also establish FCC/B2 lamellar structures, phase-level stress partitioning, and differing FCC/B2 ductility. Thus an expert could reasonably investigate intermediate-temperature aging and order-controlled embrittlement. However, none discloses the specific 600°C-to-750°C ductile-brittle-ductile sequence, L12 ordering toward Ni3Al stoichiometry in the FCC domains, jagged phase-boundary-tip stress concentration, or ductile transition zones at higher aging temperature. Those elements require a substantial additional insight, so the set is suggestive but not fully reconstructive."
